course: dictionary
lesson: 11791
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. Bellows is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The blacksmith squeezed the bellows, and the fire roared hotter.» The fire needs air, so bellows must be the tool that pushes air out.
explain: Now read this: «The dog sat by the gate and bellows at the postman.» A dog does not squeeze a tool, so bellows here is the verb. It means shouts loudly. Always ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the clues before the word. A tool, a fire or a pair of handles tells you it is the noun. A person, a giant or an animal making a loud noise tells you it is the verb, which adds -s when it goes with he, she or it.
fact: Bellows are a tool that pushes a strong stream of air out through a small opening.
fact: Blacksmiths used bellows to blow air into fires, so the fire burned hotter and could melt metal.
fact: The folding air part of an accordion or an organ is also called bellows.
fact: «Bellows» is the -s form of the verb «bellow», which means to shout or roar loudly.
fact: Our lungs work a bit like bellows, pushing air in and out.
exercise: «The blacksmith worked the bellows until the fire glowed white.» What are the bellows? | A type of metal | A kind of bell that rings in the forge | *A tool that blows air into a fire | A loud shout from the blacksmith
exercise: «The angry giant bellows, "Get out of my cave!"» What does bellows mean here? | Folds up slowly | *Shouts loudly | Whispers softly | Melts metal
exercise: «The coach bellows instructions across the field.» Find and copy one word that means to shout loudly. | *bellows | coach | field | across
test: «The accordion player pulled the bellows wide, and a happy tune filled the room.» What do the bellows do in an accordion? | Shout loudly at the audience | Ring like a bell | Hold the music sheets | *Fold in and out to push air through the reeds
test: «Her dad bellows, "Dinner is ready!" from the kitchen.» What is bellows in this sentence? | A kind of door | A part of an organ that makes music | A tool for making a fire | *A verb: he shouts loudly
exam: Why does a fire burn hotter when a blacksmith works the bellows? | The bellows cool the metal down | Air makes the fire go out | The fire needs less air to grow | *Bellows push more air into the fire, so it burns hotter
